<title>USA: Digital Biometrics gets Scottish contract.</title>
<headline>Digital Biometrics gets Scottish contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNETONKA, Minn. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Biometrics Inc, a manufacturer of identification systems, said Monday it received a major contract with French-based SAGEM SA to provide live-scan fingerprinting technology to the Scottish Police Service.</p>
<p>The value was not disclosed.</p>
<p>The contract will provide 32 S-Series Tenprinter systems through SAGEM as the prime contractor.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
